            <ArticleTitle>Schwannoma of the conus medullaris.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>80-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a rare case of schwannoma of the conus medullaris. A 38-year-old female presented with pain and numbness in her lower limbs. Magnetic resonance imaging confirmed a heterogenous tumour of the conus medullaris. A subtotal resection was performed and histology confirmed schwannoma. The literature regarding these rare tumours, and their cell of origin, is reviewed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
